media: imx6-mipi-csi2: find LINK_FREQ on the sensor behind a mux

ForgeFIRM camera bring-up (Scarthgap migration #2, milestone #5). csi2_dphy_init
reads V4L2_CID_LINK_FREQ from csi2->src_sd to pick the D-PHY hsfreqrange, but in
the Glowforge dual-camera graph a video-mux sits between the sensor and this
receiver, so src_sd (the mux) has no such control. It then falls back to the
849 Mbps default and mis-programs the D-PHY for the OV5648's ~420 Mbps output,
which manifests downstream as ipu1_csi0 EOF timeouts. Walk up the enabled links
to the sensor that publishes the control.

Upstream-Status: Pending
Signed-off-by: Scott Wiederhold <s.e.wiederhold@gmail.com>

--- a/drivers/staging/media/imx/imx6-mipi-csi2.c
+++ b/drivers/staging/media/imx/imx6-mipi-csi2.c
@@ -200,14 +200,44 @@
 	return -EINVAL;
 }
 
+/*
+ * ForgeFIRM: V4L2_CID_LINK_FREQ lives on the sensor, but in the Glowforge graph
+ * a video-mux sits between the sensor and this receiver, so csi2->src_sd (the
+ * mux) has no such control. Without it dphy_init falls back to the 849 Mbps
+ * default and mis-times the D-PHY for the OV5648's ~420 Mbps output, which shows
+ * up downstream as IPU-CSI EOF timeouts. Walk up the enabled links to the
+ * sensor that actually publishes the control.
+ */
+static struct v4l2_ctrl *csi2_find_link_freq(struct csi2_dev *csi2)
+{
+	struct v4l2_subdev *sd = csi2->src_sd;
+
+	while (sd) {
+		struct v4l2_ctrl *ctrl =
+			v4l2_ctrl_find(sd->ctrl_handler, V4L2_CID_LINK_FREQ);
+		struct media_pad *pad;
+
+		if (ctrl)
+			return ctrl;
+
+		pad = media_entity_remote_pad_unique(&sd->entity,
+						     MEDIA_PAD_FL_SOURCE);
+		if (IS_ERR_OR_NULL(pad) ||
+		    !is_media_entity_v4l2_subdev(pad->entity))
+			break;
+		sd = media_entity_to_v4l2_subdev(pad->entity);
+	}
+
+	return NULL;
+}
+
 static int csi2_dphy_init(struct csi2_dev *csi2)
 {
 	struct v4l2_ctrl *ctrl;
 	u32 mbps_per_lane;
 	int sel;
 
-	ctrl = v4l2_ctrl_find(csi2->src_sd->ctrl_handler,
-			      V4L2_CID_LINK_FREQ);
+	ctrl = csi2_find_link_freq(csi2);
 	if (!ctrl)
 		mbps_per_lane = CSI2_DEFAULT_MAX_MBPS;
